+// RewindBox (patch 0089): the pool around a texture whose upload found pages of its storage not in memory is asked ahead too. IPA 779 (Mario Kart World, iPhone17,2, races):
+//   a scene's first uploads took 136-550 ms on the submit thread (f2751: 520 textures, 97 MB, 549.8 ms, 4,164 host pages not in memory; f5467: 139, 49.6 MB, 416.6 ms, 3,518;
+//   f2346: 625, 162.5 MB, 421.6 ms), 5.6-8.5 ms for each MB read back there (2.1-2.8 ms in the IPA 777 log's largest): each upload asks its own pages (rb_wn) and its hash waits for them
+//   before the next texture's are asked, so the reads went one texture at a time (190 KB on average in f2751). The registration read-ahead found 16,722 such pages in the
+//   session against 52,699 found by the uploads: the game writes a scene's textures as it loads it, and the system writes them back to the window files and drops them before
+//   their first draw. Now such an upload also asks the 4 MB pieces of the window that hold its pool from RB_PA_BEHIND before its storage to RB_PA_AHEAD after it (the textures
+//   loaded with it lie there), its own storage left to its upload, on a serial queue of its own at QOS_CLASS_DEFAULT (I/O tier 0, as the submit thread's): their reads are in
+//   flight together while the uploads go on. A piece is asked again only RB_PA_AGAIN frames later; at most rb_pa_frame() bytes of pieces a frame (a quarter while memory is low:
+//   rb_mem_low). Pages read ahead and never used are clean file pages, which the system takes back first. What is read and uploaded does not change. The madvise runs count in
